Subject: [PATCH 1/3] harden ARM harness against @PROFDIR@ artifact pollution

Root cause of the .gcda junk that landed in a previous ms178-1.patch
revision: PGO round-trip tests carry '@PROFDIR@' placeholders in their
.flags files which only the x86 driver substitutes. The ARM differential
driver passed them through verbatim, so aarch64-gcc created a literal
'@PROFDIR@/' directory in the repo root; a later 'git add -A' swept the
binary .gcda files into a commit and hence into the format-patch.

Two defenses: (1) the ARM driver now SKIPs any test whose flags contain
@PROFDIR@ (they exercise the x86 PGO pipeline; qemu runs of them prove
nothing), and (2) '@PROFDIR@/' is gitignored so even a stray run cannot
be committed.
