   all left the store map alive; volatile allocas were tracked; escaped
   addresses (stored to memory) stayed forwardable; seg_override was
   ignored; and analysis/rewrite were two hand-kept copies that could
   drift. Ours: default-closed transfer function (only Store/Load/Memcpy
   with tracked pointers keep the map; everything else clears it),
   volatile/semantic_volatile allocas never tracked, escape analysis
   drops roots referenced outside modeled shapes (incl. variable-offset
